      "date": "1974-03-07",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "The 25-by-137.5-foot lot (3,437.5 square feet) in an R-3.5 district held a house occupied by the San Francisco Drug Treatment Program, a mainly outpatient service that had used the building for about three years. The City Planning Commission unanimously approved, with four conditions, a conditional use allowing the San Francisco Drug Treatment Program to continue occupying the building as a philanthropic institution.",
